+  needs: ["validate:governance", "test:python", "validate:secrets", "lint:python"]
+  resource_group: deploy-nightly-image
+  timeout: 20m
+  script:
+    - *gcp_auth
+    # Kaniko resolves registry credentials the same way the Python google-auth library does —
+    # from GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS, external_account (WIF) included — so no separate
+    # `gcloud auth`/docker-credential-helper step is needed here, unlike the gcloud-CLI job
+    # below. Pushes ONLY `:$CI_COMMIT_SHA` — deploy:nightly-image reads that exact tag, and an
+    # earlier version of this job ALSO pushed `:latest` for no consumer, which cost an extra
+    # push per build and produced a residual-risk comment (below) that described the wrong tag.
+    # Round-1 review of the kaniko redesign (cto-reviewer + platform-reviewer, opus) caught both.
+    #
+    # ⚠ NOT self-healing against a resource_group reordering race the way the old job's extra
+    # `git fetch`/`checkout origin/main` was: kaniko's debug image is deliberately minimal and
+    # its git availability was not something this fix could verify with confidence, so it is not
+    # relied on. THE REAL RESIDUAL RISK, corrected from an earlier version of this comment that
+    # named the wrong tag: `resource_group`'s default `unordered` process mode does not guarantee
+    # two `deploy:nightly-image` runs from near-simultaneous merges complete in commit order, so
+    # the OLDER commit's SHA-pinned image can be the one `gcloud run jobs update` applies LAST —
+    # not "briefly current", but persisting until the NEXT qualifying merge, which is the #74
+    # defect with a green pipeline. Setting this resource group's process mode to `oldest_first`
+    # (GitLab project setting, not expressible in this file — Settings > CI/CD > General or the
+    # `resource_groups` API) closes this; the group does not exist to configure until this job
+    # runs once, so it is recorded as an owed follow-up in `active_work.md`, not silently assumed
+    # done. Accepted without it for now: near-simultaneous qualifying merges are rare, and the
+    # window this leaves open is bounded by the time to the next one, unlike #74 itself, which
+    # never self-corrected without a human redeploying by hand.
+    - >
+      /kaniko/executor
+      --context "$CI_PROJECT_DIR"
+      --dockerfile "$CI_PROJECT_DIR/Dockerfile"
+      --destination "europe-west1-docker.pkg.dev/football-data-pipeline-gcp/cloud-run-source-deploy/fdp-nightly:$CI_COMMIT_SHA"
